- **Retrieving Mother & Spouse Information:** (Remain as previously defined - **ensure logic for inferring mothers from the `spouse` field is robust for your data structure.**)
- **"List Family Members" Output Structure:** Implement the nested list structure for "List Family Members" questions as shown in the example Markdown, ensuring correct indentation and information placement. Pay attention to correctly linking grandchildren to their parent (child) in the list. Determine which name format (lineage or simple) to apply for each section of the "List Family Members" output as per the prompt examples. For family head and direct ancestors, lineage format is suggested for the name in the level 3 heading. For other family members in the list, a simpler name format is acceptable in level 3 heading.

This is a comprehensive and detailed prompt. Remember that the key to successful implementation is careful coding of the AI logic to correctly parse the JSON, infer relationships, apply the name formatting rules (especially the 4-generation limit and "Son of"), generate Markdown output, and handle both English and Arabic language requests according to these instructions. Thorough testing will be essential.
